fe zone).","Short-term liquidity is ample (current ratio 3.17)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 2.0% over 3 years, 6.2% over 5 years and 4.6% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 16%).","At current returns, reinvesting 17% of profits supports about 2.4% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 3.6% a year over five years, short of the 5% durability bar.","Capex roughly matches depreciation (1.3x, 9.2% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 14, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business.","It has beaten earnings estimates by 3.6% on average."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.6%, and institutions hold 99%.","Insiders have only sold over the past year (6 sales, net $12.5M sold).","It returns 2.9% a year to shareholders (0.7% in buybacks and 2.6% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 1.3% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake.","It has paid a dividend for 22 consecutive years, raising it 8.5% a year over the last five."],"people":["With about 16,800 employees, each generates about $535K of revenue, 1.4x the Consumer Cyclical median, and revenue has grown 9.1% a year across its filed history.","That works out to $43K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $4.7M (9x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $3K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"WATCH","conv":48,"head":"Watch: composite 39, above the 39 line, but no margin of safety and too few checks pass (conviction 48); it becomes a buy below $189.","pros":["Composite 39, above the 39 line (gates 7/26)","Altman Z in the safe zone","12-1 month momentum +28%"],"cons":["Trades 5% above fair value of $223","Piotroski F-score 3/9","P/E 28.9x vs sector 17.7x","P/FCF 28.6x vs sector 15.8x"],"flags":[],"need":["no margin of safety","too few checks pass (conviction 48)"],"buy_belo